"Metode analisis area": "Area analysis method",
"Semua raster dibaca pada grid asli 0,00025° tanpa resampling; piksel masuk bila pusatnya di dalam batas; luas piksel geodesik. Kode: scripts/analisis_inti.py di https://github.com/erikprcfi/hotspot-fire-prcf (sama untuk area dampingan dan SHP unggahan).": "All rasters are read on the native 0.00025° grid without resampling; a pixel is included if its centre lies inside the boundary; geodesic pixel area. Code: scripts/analisis_inti.py at https://github.com/erikprcfi/hotspot-fire-prcf (same for assisted areas and uploaded SHPs).",
"Van Wagner, C.E. (1987) Development and Structure of the Canadian Forest Fire Weather Index System; de Groot dkk. (2006) Fire Danger Rating System Indonesia (dipakai BMKG). Input cuaca ERA5 (Copernicus C3S) dan analisis ECMWF.": "Van Wagner, C.E. (1987) Development and Structure of the Canadian Forest Fire Weather Index System; de Groot et al. (2006) Fire Danger Rating System Indonesia (used by BMKG). Weather input from ERA5 (Copernicus C3S) and ECMWF analysis.",
"Satelit mendeteksi panas saat melintas (beberapa kali sehari); api kecil, singkat, atau di bawah tajuk dan saat tertutup awan dapat tidak terdeteksi. Luas terbakar perlu diukur dengan analisa citra (burn scar) atau lapangan.": "Satellites detect heat as they pass over (several times a day); small, short-lived or under-canopy fires and fires under cloud cover may go undetected. Burned area must be measured with image analysis (burn scars) or in the field.",
