"Indeks bahaya kebakaran harian (FDRS)": "Daily fire danger index (FDRS)",
"Tingkat bahaya kebakaran harian dihitung dengan Canadian Fire Weather Index System (Van Wagner 1987) dari data cuaca analisis ERA5/ECMWF di pusat lokasi, dengan kelas Fire Danger Rating System Indonesia (de Groot dkk. 2006; dipakai BMKG): tingkat harian = kelas tertinggi dari FFMC (bahan bakar halus) dan DC (kekeringan lapisan dalam). Data tersedia": "The daily fire danger level is calculated with the Canadian Fire Weather Index System (Van Wagner 1987) from ERA5/ECMWF analysis weather data at the site centre, with the Fire Danger Rating System Indonesia classes (de Groot et al. 2006; used by BMKG): daily level = the highest class of FFMC (fine fuels) and DC (deep-layer drought). Data available for",
