"Sumber: Forest GHG emissions, removals & net flux #–# (Harris et al. #, Nat. Clim. Change; Gibbs et al. #, ESSD), versi #, data publik World Resources Institute, CC BY #; Stok karbon hutan tahun # (Harris et al. #), versi #, CC BY #. Emisi bruto mencakup CO#, CH# dan N#O dari biomassa dan tanah (termasuk gambut) akibat hilangnya tutupan pohon; serapan bruto = penyerapan CO# oleh hutan yang tetap/tumbuh; fluks bersih = emisi - serapan (negatif = penyerap karbon bersih). Nilai per tahun = total # tahun ÷ #. Ini hasil model global dengan ketidakpastian; bukan pengganti inventarisasi karbon/MRV lapangan.": "Source: Forest GHG emissions, removals & net flux #–# (Harris et al. #, Nat. Clim. Change; Gibbs et al. #, ESSD), version #, World Resources Institute public data, CC BY #; Forest carbon stock in # (Harris et al. #), version #, CC BY #. Gross emissions include CO#, CH# and N#O from biomass and soil (including peat) caused by tree cover loss; gross removals = CO# uptake by standing/growing forest; net flux = emissions - removals (negative = net carbon sink). Value per year = # year total ÷ #. These are global model results with uncertainty; not a substitute for a field carbon inventory/MRV.",
"Jumlah deteksi titik panas tipe vegetasi dari arsip tahunan final NASA FIRMS di dalam batas Hutan Desa dan wilayah desa (VIIRS S-NPP, VIIRS NOAA-#, MODIS). Hanya deteksi tipe # (dugaan kebakaran vegetasi). Satu kebakaran bisa terdeteksi oleh beberapa satelit/lintasan, jadi jumlah titik ≠ jumlah kejadian. Arsip tahunan NASA untuk tahun berjalan belum terbit.": "Number of vegetation-type hotspot detections from the final NASA FIRMS annual archive within the Village Forest and village boundaries (VIIRS S-NPP, VIIRS NOAA-#, MODIS). Only type # detections (suspected vegetation fires). One fire can be detected by several satellites/passes, so the number of hotspots ≠ the number of events. The NASA annual archive for the current year has not been published yet.",
